---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Csapat from '../../components/Csapat.astro';
---

<Base cim="About us – Triox Informatika" leiras="More than 20 years of enterprise IT operations experience, our own server fleet, and a personal relationship with the people who run your systems.">
  <article class="band">
    <div class="wrap-szeles">

      <p class="eyebrow">About us</p>
      <h1>We know how to help you.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Triox Informatika is a Hungarian hosting and infrastructure operations provider. On servers we own and operate, we deliver virtualized and physical environments to business clients—on a network that is dedicated and isolated per client.</p>

      <section class="blokk">
        <h2>Behind Triox</h2>
        <p>We have been running corporate IT systems since 2003. Over more than twenty years, our responsibilities have grown as well: today our own, fully operated server fleet sits in two independent, ISO 27001-certified data centers in Budapest, on a redundant 2×10 Gbps backbone. That is why we can deliver from a single source what usually takes several providers: leased infrastructure, full data center outsourcing, application hosting and day-to-day operations.</p>
        <p>We work quietly, but the stakes are not small. Clients trust us with environments where an outage would stop a live broadcast aired nationwide, a compute-intensive medical research project, or customer service in more than 400 branches across Hungary.</p>
        <p>With us, you deal with names and faces, not ticket numbers—the two of us are responsible for making sure that what we promise to our partners and suppliers actually gets delivered.</p>
        <Csapat />
      </section>

      <section class="blokk">
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>We don't sell templates. Every client's environment is unique, so we tailor both the infrastructure and the operations service to the specific needs.</p>
        <p>In practice, this means that <strong>every client runs on its own separate network segment</strong>, with a dedicated gateway and its own firewall and NAT rules. You share it with no one, and you don't get a common template applied to everyone.</p>
        <p><strong>Our service models:</strong></p>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Model</th><th>What it means</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>IaaS</strong></td><td>Leased virtual infrastructure—virtual machines, storage, networking</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>DCaaS</strong></td><td>The client's entire data center, outsourced to our sites</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>SaaS</strong></td><td>Hosting of business applications in a managed environment</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Managed IT operations</strong></td><td>Not just the server, but the operations team too—a single partner for all of your IT</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <section class="blokk">
        <h2>Technical experience</h2>
        <p>Through its employees, contract partners and subcontractors, our company covers a wide range of operating systems, networks and database systems. We work every day with the technologies a company may encounter in the course of its operations.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Virtualization</strong> – Microsoft Hyper-V, VMware, Proxmox</li>
          <li><strong>Server environments</strong> – Windows Server and Linux, Active Directory, directory services</li>
          <li><strong>Databases</strong> – operating SQL and application databases</li>
          <li><strong>Networking</strong> – VLAN-based and physical segmentation, firewall, VPN, redundant 2×10 Gbps backbone</li>
          <li><strong>Cloud</strong> – Microsoft 365 and Azure, hybrid environments</li>
          <li><strong>Backup and recovery</strong> – enterprise-grade data backup, off-site replication, documented restore tests</li>
          <li><strong>Security</strong> – endpoint protection, multi-factor authentication, out-of-band management, regular infrastructure audits</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="blokk">
        <h2>High return on investment</h2>
        <p><strong>Are you spending too much on running your current systems?</strong></p>
        <p>More and more businesses are realizing that ongoing IT operations, along with researching and adopting new technologies, consume a significant share of their revenue. Maintaining your own server room, replacing hardware, licenses and dependence on a single system administrator together add up to a cost and a risk that is rarely seen as a whole.</p>
        <p>By outsourcing your IT processes, these costs become <strong>predictable and can be reduced significantly</strong>—and you only need to focus on what you do best.</p>
        <p><strong>What outsourcing gives you:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>a predictable monthly fee instead of ad hoc, unexpected bills</li>
          <li>no single-person risk—a team stands behind it, not a single colleague</li>
          <li>a documented environment where the knowledge is not kept in one person's head</li>
          <li>prevention instead of firefighting</li>
          <li>a single accountable partner who doesn't point fingers at others</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="blokk">
        <h2>Satisfaction guarantee</h2>
        <p>Seen from the outside, the world of IT changes alarmingly fast. Our primary goal is to take that burden off our clients—with professional, personalized service and high-quality technical execution.</p>
        <p><strong>How we work:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Personal contact</strong> – real specialists, not ticket numbers</li>
          <li><strong>Hungarian-language support</strong> – clear explanations, no jargon</li>
          <li><strong>Transparency</strong> – a documented environment and regular reports filtered to your own environment</li>
          <li><strong>No rigid packages</strong> – custom configuration, not prebuilt templates</li>
          <li><strong>Provable operation</strong> – a backup is only worth something if it can actually be restored; we test and document this</li>
        </ul>
        <blockquote>We guarantee that you will be satisfied with our work. <strong>Because we know how to help you.</strong></blockquote>
      </section>

      <section class="blokk">
        <h2>By the numbers</h2>
        <table class="szamok">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Since 2003</strong></td><td>operating in Budapest</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>20+ years</strong></td><td>of enterprise IT operations experience</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>2</strong></td><td>data center sites in Budapest</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>2×10 Gbps</strong></td><td>redundant backbone</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>1 client = 1 network</strong></td><td>client-level isolation with a dedicated gateway</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <section class="blokk">
        <h2>Who we work with</h2>
        <p>We do not publish our clients' names—in the projects below, the problem we solved is what matters.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Nationwide media provider</strong>—complete internal network, web and data infrastructure</li>
          <li><strong>Biotechnology research lab</strong>—fully isolated IT infrastructure handling large volumes of data</li>
          <li><strong>Financial services provider with a nationwide branch network</strong>—two-tier, segmented application stack</li>
          <li><strong>Commercial and service companies</strong>—web, file and directory environments</li>
        </ul>
        <p><a href="/en/case-studies/">Case studies →</a></p>
      </section>

      <section class="blokk">
        <h2>Feel free to get in touch</h2>
        <div class="kapcsolat-grid">
          <div>
            <p><strong>Triox Informatika Kft.</strong><br>
            1106 Budapest, Kada utca 133.<br>
            Tax ID: 13316460-2-42<br>
            Company registration no.: 01-09-449388</p>
            <p>Email: <a href="mailto:info@triox.hu">info@triox.hu</a></p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p><strong>Data center sites</strong><br>
            1138 Budapest, Váci út 188.<br>
            1132 Budapest, Victor Hugo utca 18–22. (BIX)</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top:2rem"><a class="btn" href="/en/contact/">Contact form</a></p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .wrap-szeles {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--w-max);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--pad);
    padding-block: 3rem;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--c-steel);
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .blokk {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--c-line);
  }

  .blokk h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .blokk ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .blokk li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .blokk blockquote {
    border-left: 4px solid var(--c-brand);
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--c-brand-wash);
    border-radius: 0 var(--r) var(--r) 0;
    color: var(--c-ink);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.93rem;
    margin-block: 1.25rem;
  }

  th, td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--c-line);
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  th {
    background: var(--c-ink);
    color: #e9ecf2;
    font-family: var(--f-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  tr:nth-child(even) td {
    background: var(--c-mist);
  }

  .szamok td:first-child {
    font-family: var(--f-display);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
    width: 12rem;
  }

  .kapcsolat-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    table {
      display: block;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }

    .kapcsolat-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
